 "circuits": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Inside the part",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "A voltage reference feeds an error amplifier, which compares it with a resistor divider from VOUT to GND and, through a driver, controls a PNP pass transistor from VIN to VOUT. A sense resistor ahead of the pass transistor feeds a current-limit block. A start-up and shutdown block driven by SHDN, and a thermal-protection block, act on the regulation loop. The Bypass pin connects to the reference output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Parts with outputs above 2 V operate from VOUT + 0.5 V up to 14 V; parts below 2 V operate from 2.5 V to 14 V. The input may reach 16 V without damage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Shutdown",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "SHDN accepts TTL or CMOS levels. The output is on with SHDN at 1.8 V or more and off at 0.6 V or less, or with the pin grounded. SHDN may be taken to 16 V. With it at 1.8 V the pin sinks 12 µA typical, 35 µA at most, and the current rises with the pin voltage to about 59 µA at 5 V. Off, the regulator draws 0.1 µA at most. The typical thresholds fall with temperature: about 1.5 V (on) and 1.36 V (off) at -40 °C, about 0.97 V and 0.69 V at 80 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Noise bypass",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "A capacitor from the Bypass pin sets the output noise: 30 µVrms from 10 Hz to 80 kHz with 0.1 µF, at IO = 60 mA and CO = 10 µF. Without it the noise density near 1 kHz is around 400 nV/√Hz to 590 nV/√Hz; with 100 nF it is about 90 nV/√Hz to 110 nV/√Hz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part monitors its load current and shuts down on a short circuit or an overcurrent. The current limit is 150 mA at least; the short-circuit current is about 0.30 A for a 2.5 V part. Thermal shutdown keeps the junction under 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Quiescent current",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Unloaded and on, the part draws 175 µA typical, 250 µA at most. Ground current rises with load, to about 1.6 mA at 100 mA (VO = 3.8 V). In shutdown it is 0 µA typical, 0.1 µA at most at VI = 8 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output capacitor",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "The regulator is stable with output capacitance from about 0.6 µF to about 19 µF and ESR from about 0.03 Ω to about 20 Ω. The electrical characteristics are measured with CI = 1 µF and CO = 2.2 µF."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Reverse current",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "With VI = 0, the reverse current of a 3.8 V part rises about linearly with reverse voltage, to about 200 µA at 16 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "In SOT23-5L, junction-to-case resistance is 81 °C/W and junction-to-ambient is 255 °C/W. The GND pin is the heat path from the die flag. The junction may run from -40 °C to 125 °C."
  }
 ],
